    {
      "type": "e_vehicle_battery",
      "description": "Ride for up to 100 km with its hidden 250 Wh battery.; The 250 Wh battery integrated into the frame provides a maximum battery range of 100 km to let the miles fly by. The optional battery extender (eX1, 171Wh), which fits discreetly into one of the bottle cages, extends the maximum range to 150km for all-day rides. Naturally, battery life will drop based on the assistance level used, the route, the cyclist's weight, the temperature, the wind, etc.; powerful front and rear lighting powered by the bike's battery; fully-integrated diagonal tube battery; Mahle 36V 250Wh; Compatible with the battery extender available for bottle cage (eX1, 171Wh) (not included)"
    },
    {
      "type": "e_vehicle_motor",
      "description": "Light, compact Mahle X30 motor with three levels of assistance and 45Nm torque.; The Mahle X30 assistance system on our electric gravel bike amplifies your effort up to 45 Nm, allowing you to overcome the toughest obstacles thanks to the three levels of assistance to choose from. However, it knows how to be discreet with its battery built into the frame and its weight of just 3.5 kg, making it nearly imperceptible when you don't need it.; Mahle X30 rear hub motor; 36V – 250w, 45N.m; up to 25km/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "e_vehicle_remote",
      "manufacturer": "Mahle",
      "description": "Mahle Pulsar One display, a computer that communicates wirelessly with your bike; Wireless, the new Mahle PulsarONE cycle computer enables you to interact with your bike and gives you access to data such as speed and distance, remaining battery life, chosen level of assistance, and so on.; Take control of your electric bike! You can increase or decrease the level of assistance and control the lights."
